It is possible that an opioid-continuation possibly initiates a long-term-opioid-therapy after 30 days.
If a clinician does not provably make an intentional-benefit-risk-decision with a patient then it is recommended that the clinician does not initiate a long-term-opioid-therapy.
If a clinician does not provably conduct an informed-discussion with a patient then it is recommended that the clinician does not initiate a long-term-opioid-therapy.
If a clinician does not provably use a comprehensive-pain-management then it is recommended that the clinician does not initiate a long-term-opioid-therapy.
